<section class="policy-hero"><div class="policy-wrap"><h1>Terms of Use</h1><p>Important information about use of the Livermore Lions Rugby Club website.</p></div></section><section class="policy-main"><div class="policy-wrap">
<p class="policy-meta"><strong>Effective date:</strong> August 19, 2026</p>
<h2>1. Purpose of this website</h2><p>This website provides general information about Livermore Lions Rugby Club, youth rugby programs, schedules, volunteering, and registration. Information may change as fixtures, governing-body requirements, age grades, venues, and club operations change.</p>
<h2>2. Registration</h2><p>Submitting an enquiry or club intake form does not itself complete official rugby registration. Players must complete any required Rugby Xplorer, Rugby NorCal, USA Rugby, insurance, waiver, fee, or other registration steps before participating where required.</p>
<h2>3. Parent or guardian use</h2><p>Forms requesting information about a minor are intended to be completed by the child’s parent or legal guardian. Children should not submit personal information directly through this website.</p>
<h2>4. Safety</h2><p>Rugby and athletic activities involve inherent risks. Participation is subject to applicable waivers, governing-body requirements, club rules, coaching instructions, and player-welfare procedures. Website content is not medical advice.</p>
<h2>5. Third-party services</h2><p>The website may link to Rugby Xplorer, Rugby NorCal, social media, mapping services, or other third-party services. Their terms and privacy practices are controlled by those third parties.</p>
<h2>6. Website content</h2><p>Club names, logos, artwork, photographs, and original website content may not be reproduced for commercial use without permission. Third-party marks remain the property of their respective owners.</p>
<h2>7. Availability and accuracy</h2><p>We try to keep schedules and club information accurate, but training times, venues, fixtures, age-grade details, and other information may change. Parents and players should check current club communications before traveling to an activity.</p>
<h2>8. Contact</h2><p>Questions can be sent to <strong>hello@livermorerugby.com</strong>.</p>
</div></section>
